1
00:00:00,933 --> 00:00:04,300
That book you wrote,
"An Animal's First Sight".

2
00:00:05,266 --> 00:00:06,866
I still remember how it begins.

3
00:00:08,666 --> 00:00:09,666
You wrote

4
00:00:09,766 --> 00:00:11,733
that when small animals are born

5
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:14,966
the first living creature they see

6
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:17,200
they take to be their mother

7
00:00:17,486 --> 00:00:20,586
following close behind, growing attached.

8
00:00:22,100 --> 00:00:24,133
In those days when you couldn't see,

9
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:26,266
I loved the way you

10
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:31,726
clung to me without holding
back, like some lost little animal,

11
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:33,700
and followed me.

12
00:00:34,700 --> 00:00:36,266
But I know

13
00:00:36,366 --> 00:00:38,933
we're more like parallel universes
in a movie

14
00:00:40,533 --> 00:00:44,066
where the other half of us lives.

15
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:47,766
Fifteen years ago

16
00:00:47,866 --> 00:00:50,533
my stepfather kept calling me
the wrong name.

17
00:00:51,333 --> 00:00:52,932
I used to think

18
00:00:52,933 --> 00:00:56,766
that wrong name had to be
the other half of me.

19
00:00:58,066 --> 00:01:01,666
Even if fate means
I vanish from your world...

20
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:06,266
It's been fifteen years

21
00:01:06,333 --> 00:01:07,766
and all I want this summer

22
00:01:09,333 --> 00:01:10,466
is to see you…

23
00:01:39,633 --> 00:01:40,633
Hey.

24
00:01:47,100 --> 00:01:49,365
You want to sleep, go sleep somewhere else

25
00:01:49,366 --> 00:01:50,600
I'm running a business here.

26
00:01:51,100 --> 00:01:55,332
Aw, come on boss lady,
I'm seriously good at this.

27
00:01:55,333 --> 00:01:56,600
Just give me room and board

28
00:01:57,100 --> 00:01:58,366
and pay me whatever you want.

29
00:01:59,500 --> 00:02:01,666
I used to work for your family

30
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:04,166
and now you want to be my waiter?

31
00:02:04,300 --> 00:02:07,233
Just go back to Singapore
and be the young master.

32
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:08,900
Come on, Yong Qi

33
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:11,500
my dad cut off all my credit cards.

34
00:02:11,933 --> 00:02:12,966
Do me a favor

35
00:02:13,233 --> 00:02:14,533
and take me in for a bit.

36
00:02:14,633 --> 00:02:16,533
Can I take that kind of responsibility?

37
00:02:16,566 --> 00:02:18,433
You graduate in a few months

38
00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:20,599
and you cut class to come to the mainland.

39
00:02:20,600 --> 00:02:22,600
Song Yi, what are you really after?

40
00:02:23,333 --> 00:02:25,733
Uh, for you, of course.

41
00:02:25,966 --> 00:02:26,966
Heh heh.

42
00:02:27,333 --> 00:02:28,733
Messing with me, are you?

43
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:29,566
Fine

44
00:02:29,766 --> 00:02:31,699
I'm calling Mr. Song right now.

45
00:02:31,700 --> 00:02:32,400
Hey!

46
00:02:32,666 --> 00:02:35,366
Sis, give me a break.

47
00:02:35,766 --> 00:02:37,600
If my old man finds out I'm here

48
00:02:37,700 --> 00:02:39,833
he'd disown me for sure.

49
00:02:41,033 --> 00:02:44,366
Song Yi, is all this really necessary?

50
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:50,100
Actually… I came here to find someone.

51
00:02:50,333 --> 00:02:51,399
Find someone?

52
00:02:51,400 --> 00:02:53,733
Hurry up and find them, then get going!

53
00:02:54,666 --> 00:02:54,833
Hey

54
00:02:55,100 --> 00:02:56,633
I don't have any leads yet.

55
00:02:56,966 --> 00:02:58,932
Around here, other than me

56
00:02:58,933 --> 00:03:00,266
who else do you even know?

57
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:06,333
Don't tell me you fell for a romance scam

58
00:03:06,500 --> 00:03:07,500
and got conned?

59
00:03:10,209 --> 00:03:11,508
Maybe I did.

60
00:03:11,533 --> 00:03:14,266
I'm warning you, you'd better behave.

61
00:03:14,333 --> 00:03:16,800
Right now I count as half your guardian.

62
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:20,800
So, does that mean I can stay?

63
00:03:27,633 --> 00:03:29,766
Thanks, bye.

64
00:03:42,133 --> 00:03:44,666
Sorry, I didn't know you…

65
00:03:51,900 --> 00:03:53,600
I was just trying to help.

66
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:55,566
Did you have to react like that?

67
00:03:55,900 --> 00:03:56,966
I do not need your help.

68
00:04:01,100 --> 00:04:03,532
Feiyu, what are you doing here?

69
00:04:03,533 --> 00:04:05,133
You okay? Are you hurt?

70
00:04:05,233 --> 00:04:06,233
Hm?

71
00:04:07,633 --> 00:04:08,733
Did you do this?

72
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:10,466
I didn't do anything!

73
00:04:16,233 --> 00:04:19,265
It's nearly three kilometers,
how did you get here?

74
00:04:19,266 --> 00:04:20,266
That's dangerous!

75
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:21,666
I'm fine.

76
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:23,733
Where's the caregiver I found for you?

77
00:04:23,800 --> 00:04:25,032
She didn't come with you?

78
00:04:25,033 --> 00:04:26,300
She resigned.

79
00:04:26,493 --> 00:04:27,659
I'm fine on my own.

80
00:04:27,800 --> 00:04:28,700
I don't need one.

81
00:04:28,701 --> 00:04:30,633
You drove her off again, didn't you.

82
00:04:30,666 --> 00:04:31,733
Fine.

83
00:04:31,993 --> 00:04:35,159
Another spoiled prince to wait on.

84
00:04:35,333 --> 00:04:35,800
Hey.

85
00:04:36,066 --> 00:04:37,200
Don't look at me.

86
00:04:37,333 --> 00:04:38,866
Nobody's easier to get along with.

87
00:04:40,333 --> 00:04:40,900
Come on.

88
00:04:40,900 --> 00:04:41,500
Go on in

89
00:04:41,501 --> 00:04:42,833
I'll get the kitchen to cook.

90
00:04:43,333 --> 00:04:44,200
Thank you.

91
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:45,200
Wow.

92
00:04:46,233 --> 00:04:48,132
The way she treats people

93
00:04:48,133 --> 00:04:52,499
it's like night and day!

94
00:04:52,500 --> 00:04:53,566
He's in that condition

95
00:04:53,733 --> 00:04:54,933
and you're making comparisons?

96
00:04:54,966 --> 00:04:55,966
Come on.

97
00:04:57,900 --> 00:04:58,933
Hey, senior.

98
00:04:59,600 --> 00:05:00,766
I haven't eaten yet.

99
00:05:00,966 --> 00:05:02,400
I'm starving too.

100
00:05:07,100 --> 00:05:08,100
Careful now.

101
00:05:11,100 --> 00:05:12,100
Feiyu.

102
00:05:12,400 --> 00:05:14,399
From now on, don't come here alone.

103
00:05:14,400 --> 00:05:15,832
The road's full of traffic.

104
00:05:15,833 --> 00:05:16,833
It's too dangerous.

105
00:05:19,266 --> 00:05:20,266
Mm.

106
00:05:20,533 --> 00:05:21,533
Wait here.

107
00:05:46,933 --> 00:05:48,133
What are you doing?

108
00:05:49,100 --> 00:05:52,133
I... I'm waiting for my food.

109
00:05:53,733 --> 00:05:56,766
I don't like sharing a table
with strangers.

110
00:05:57,900 --> 00:06:00,165
Then you can go sit at another table.

111
00:06:00,166 --> 00:06:01,300
Nobody's stopping you.

112
00:06:05,100 --> 00:06:07,399
Hey, wait, wait, wait.

113
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:09,900
I'll move, I'll move. Happy now?

114
00:06:33,333 --> 00:06:35,700
So what's the deal with you and Yong Qi?

115
00:06:36,600 --> 00:06:37,866
Why's she so nice to you?

116
00:06:46,600 --> 00:06:47,700
I'll introduce myself.

117
00:06:48,300 --> 00:06:49,566
I'm Yong Qi's junior.

118
00:06:54,133 --> 00:06:55,600
What're you two talking about?

119
00:06:57,666 --> 00:06:58,733
Nothing much.

120
00:06:59,066 --> 00:07:00,832
This friend of yours

121
00:07:00,833 --> 00:07:02,200
wants to share my table.

122
00:07:03,133 --> 00:07:04,033
Great.

123
00:07:04,133 --> 00:07:05,133
Then sit together.

124
00:07:10,233 --> 00:07:12,100
Feiyu, let me introduce you.

125
00:07:12,366 --> 00:07:13,492
This is...

126
00:07:13,505 --> 00:07:14,045
I know.

127
00:07:14,333 --> 00:07:15,333
Your junior.

128
00:07:16,300 --> 00:07:19,633
Mm, right. His name's Song Yi.

129
00:07:19,733 --> 00:07:22,066
My junior from
National University of Singapore.

130
00:07:22,166 --> 00:07:24,933
I worked part-time at
his family's Japanese restaurant.

131
00:07:25,333 --> 00:07:28,166
Song Yi, this is Xu Feiyu.

132
00:07:29,066 --> 00:07:32,800
His mother and I are... good friends.

133
00:07:33,266 --> 00:07:34,266
Got it.

134
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:36,066
So he's my nephew.

135
00:07:40,866 --> 00:07:44,533
Feiyu, I'm finding you
another caregiver today.

136
00:07:45,300 --> 00:07:47,033
Don't you chase this one away too.

137
00:07:47,233 --> 00:07:49,666
I've got to answer to your mother,
you know.

138
00:07:50,866 --> 00:07:51,866
Do what you want.

139
00:07:53,433 --> 00:07:56,133
The restaurant's about to get busy,
Song Yi.

140
00:07:56,800 --> 00:07:59,966
After you eat, take Feiyu home for me.

141
00:08:00,200 --> 00:08:01,200
Me!?

142
00:08:02,533 --> 00:08:03,533
No, thank you.

143
00:08:03,966 --> 00:08:05,633
I can get home by myself.

144
00:08:06,266 --> 00:08:07,533
See? You heard him.

145
00:08:07,700 --> 00:08:10,266
My nephew says
he doesn't need a ride home.

146
00:08:11,200 --> 00:08:14,233
What's with everyone today?
All fighting me.

147
00:08:16,766 --> 00:08:19,032
Hey— wait, wait, wait.

148
00:08:19,033 --> 00:08:20,933
I'll take him, I'll take him.

149
00:08:21,533 --> 00:08:23,799
I'll get him home safe, guaranteed.

150
00:08:23,800 --> 00:08:26,300
If anything happens to Feiyu, it's on you.

151
00:08:26,900 --> 00:08:28,033
Don't worry.

152
00:08:28,466 --> 00:08:30,066
Consider it done.

153
00:08:30,133 --> 00:08:31,133
Ngh—.

154
00:08:32,066 --> 00:08:33,966
Feiyu, are you okay?

155
00:08:34,933 --> 00:08:37,400
Song Yi, just get him home, that's all.

156
00:08:37,500 --> 00:08:40,365
He doesn't like strangers touching him,
so don't.

157
00:08:40,366 --> 00:08:41,366
Got it?

158
00:08:41,666 --> 00:08:42,666
Fine.

159
00:08:58,633 --> 00:09:01,666
Whoa! Private villa. Somebody's rich.

160
00:09:05,600 --> 00:09:12,533
Easy— watch your step.

161
00:09:16,233 --> 00:09:17,465
You may go now.

162
00:09:17,466 --> 00:09:19,232
I brought you all this way—

163
00:09:19,233 --> 00:09:21,565
and you won't even invite me in?

164
00:09:21,566 --> 00:09:22,566
No.

165
00:09:24,466 --> 00:09:25,500
Oh, come on—.

166
00:09:26,800 --> 00:09:30,400
I walked all this way in the blazing sun,
soaked in sweat.

167
00:09:31,900 --> 00:09:33,799
You won't invite me in,

168
00:09:33,800 --> 00:09:34,500
at least

169
00:09:34,501 --> 00:09:35,900
be a bit more polite.

170
00:09:37,100 --> 00:09:39,566
Thank you for your trouble.
Please go home.

171
00:09:43,700 --> 00:09:46,732
You— I— What, do I owe you something?!

172
00:09:46,733 --> 00:09:47,733
Tch!

173
00:10:14,700 --> 00:10:15,133
Hey.

174
00:10:15,333 --> 00:10:16,333
What're you looking at?

175
00:10:17,733 --> 00:10:18,733
Nothing.

176
00:10:20,300 --> 00:10:21,300
Right, Yong Qi—

177
00:10:21,633 --> 00:10:22,633
that Xu Feiyu guy—

178
00:10:22,866 --> 00:10:24,100
is he hiring a caregiver?

179
00:10:24,166 --> 00:10:25,166
Yeah.

180
00:10:25,433 --> 00:10:27,033
He just had iris surgery,

181
00:10:27,233 --> 00:10:29,500
and his mom's away on business in Europe,

182
00:10:29,900 --> 00:10:31,800
so she asked me to find him a caregiver.

183
00:10:32,333 --> 00:10:34,266
Her son has surgery and she's flying abroad.

184
00:10:35,033 --> 00:10:36,466
Is she really his mother?

185
00:10:37,600 --> 00:10:38,800
Don't talk nonsense.

186
00:10:39,033 --> 00:10:39,833
No, no—

187
00:10:39,834 --> 00:10:41,465
I'm just joking.

188
00:10:41,466 --> 00:10:43,400
So can you let me give it a try?

189
00:10:45,266 --> 00:10:46,266
Try what?

190
00:10:46,333 --> 00:10:47,366
The caregiver job.

191
00:10:48,400 --> 00:10:49,432
You?

192
00:10:49,433 --> 00:10:50,433
Yeah!

193
00:10:50,566 --> 00:10:52,132
Forget it, rich boy.

194
00:10:52,133 --> 00:10:53,800
You're more trouble than Feiyu.

195
00:10:54,133 --> 00:10:57,133
I kept a whole house full of pets
in Singapore.

196
00:10:57,400 --> 00:11:00,576
Looking after one fish— shouldn't be a problem.
[TN: Feiyu's name sounds like flying fish]

197
00:11:00,600 --> 00:11:01,600
Quit messing around.

198
00:11:01,900 --> 00:11:04,833
Then go back to Singapore
and look after your pets.

199
00:11:05,666 --> 00:11:07,000
Yong Qi.

200
00:11:08,700 --> 00:11:09,999
I'm serious.

201
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:12,033
Besides, we're about the same age

202
00:11:12,400 --> 00:11:13,933
we'd get along just fine.

203
00:11:15,300 --> 00:11:16,565
Get along?

204
00:11:16,566 --> 00:11:17,566
Yeah.

205
00:11:18,266 --> 00:11:21,000
You have no idea how difficult he is.

206
00:11:21,466 --> 00:11:22,466
Plus

207
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:25,132
he has haphephobia

208
00:11:25,133 --> 00:11:26,633
scared of strangers touching him

209
00:11:26,866 --> 00:11:28,366
and he's a total germaphobe.

210
00:11:29,200 --> 00:11:30,433
What weird disease is that?

211
00:11:31,500 --> 00:11:32,566
Well, no wonder.

212
00:11:33,333 --> 00:11:34,966
He was never normal to begin with.

213
00:11:36,300 --> 00:11:38,033
You're not normal either.

214
00:11:38,766 --> 00:11:39,766
Come on.

215
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:42,000
Yong Qi.

216
00:11:42,633 --> 00:11:44,466
You won't find anyone that fast anyway.

217
00:11:44,933 --> 00:11:45,700
Trust me

218
00:11:45,933 --> 00:11:47,466
nobody's a better fit than me.

219
00:11:48,533 --> 00:11:50,332
I'll go pack right now

220
00:11:50,333 --> 00:11:51,432
and start right away.

221
00:11:51,433 --> 00:11:52,433
If it doesn't work

222
00:11:52,434 --> 00:11:53,899
you can find someone else.

223
00:11:53,900 --> 00:11:54,800
Hey… hey, Song Yi…

224
00:11:54,801 --> 00:11:56,366
I'm going. It's settled.

225
00:12:06,233 --> 00:12:07,233
Who is it?

226
00:12:12,333 --> 00:12:13,866
Coming, one moment.

227
00:12:18,033 --> 00:12:19,333
Coming, coming.

228
00:12:28,066 --> 00:12:29,333
Hello, who is it?

229
00:12:34,400 --> 00:12:36,700
Who is it? Hello, is anyone there?

230
00:12:39,733 --> 00:12:40,833
Who is it?

231
00:12:41,733 --> 00:12:42,733
Anyone there?

232
00:12:43,400 --> 00:12:44,400
Hello, who is it?

233
00:12:44,700 --> 00:12:45,800
Is anyone there!

234
00:12:47,833 --> 00:12:51,333
Agh! Xu Feiyu.

235
00:12:52,066 --> 00:12:54,366
A mousetrap at your door in broad daylight.

236
00:12:54,600 --> 00:12:56,066
You psycho!

237
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:59,000
- Ow…
- You again.

238
00:12:59,233 --> 00:13:00,766
Why are you at my house again?

239
00:13:01,933 --> 00:13:04,033
I'm the new caregiver
Yong Qi found for you.

240
00:13:04,633 --> 00:13:06,766
I already told you,
I don't need a caregiver.

241
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:09,032
Hey! Even if you don't need one

242
00:13:09,033 --> 00:13:10,300
you didn't have to hurt me?

243
00:13:10,533 --> 00:13:12,366
My foot hurts too much to walk.

244
00:13:12,533 --> 00:13:14,100
This is assault.

245
00:13:14,466 --> 00:13:15,466
So you owe me.

246
00:13:16,100 --> 00:13:17,233
Owww.

247
00:13:17,933 --> 00:13:19,000
Don't go in any further.

248
00:13:20,100 --> 00:13:20,533
Hey.

249
00:13:20,766 --> 00:13:21,233
Wait.

250
00:13:21,234 --> 00:13:22,599
This is breaking and entering

251
00:13:22,600 --> 00:13:23,900
I could call the police.

252
00:13:24,500 --> 00:13:26,466
I politely rang the doorbell

253
00:13:26,533 --> 00:13:27,300
and you opened it

254
00:13:27,533 --> 00:13:28,900
so procedurally we're fine.

255
00:13:29,066 --> 00:13:30,800
At most, I'm an uninvited guest.

256
00:13:31,100 --> 00:13:32,700
But you? That's abusing your carer.

257
00:13:33,233 --> 00:13:35,832
Ow— it hurts, it hurts.

258
00:13:35,833 --> 00:13:37,266
Stop! Stop right there!

259
00:13:37,500 --> 00:13:40,766
Siri! Siri, call Yong Qi.

260
00:13:41,233 --> 00:13:41,733
Ohh.

261
00:13:41,734 --> 00:13:42,965
Get out. Nobody let you in.

262
00:13:42,966 --> 00:13:44,033
So this is the place.

263
00:13:45,016 --> 00:13:47,576
(The number you have
called cannot be connected...)

264
00:13:47,600 --> 00:13:50,333
In your condition, you can still do these.

265
00:13:50,466 --> 00:13:51,632
Doing it blind?

266
00:13:51,633 --> 00:13:52,466
Don't touch my stuff.

267
00:13:52,533 --> 00:13:54,266
Get out, right now

268
00:13:54,400 --> 00:13:56,033
I know you don't want a new carer

269
00:13:56,300 --> 00:13:57,966
I came here to solve that problem.

270
00:13:58,033 --> 00:13:59,033
Think about it.

271
00:13:59,466 --> 00:14:02,600
Your mom and Yong Qi
will never let you be alone.

272
00:14:02,866 --> 00:14:03,933
As long as I stay

273
00:14:04,066 --> 00:14:05,186
nobody will come to bug you.

274
00:14:06,166 --> 00:14:07,166
Hm?

275
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:09,333
Come on, relax

276
00:14:09,700 --> 00:14:10,966
I can be invisible.

277
00:14:11,199 --> 00:14:13,000
Unless you call,
I won't bother you.

278
00:14:18,666 --> 00:14:20,200
Hey, ca-careful.

279
00:14:24,400 --> 00:14:27,100
I'll do whatever you say,
just think about it?

280
00:14:28,233 --> 00:14:30,600
Look, let me be straight with you

281
00:14:30,933 --> 00:14:32,433
I ran away from home, I'm stranded

282
00:14:32,800 --> 00:14:33,900
and I'm flat broke

283
00:14:34,266 --> 00:14:35,933
I really do need this job.

284
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:38,100
I'm good at this stuff.

285
00:14:38,400 --> 00:14:41,000
Laundry, cooking, making beds —
I'm good at all of it.

286
00:14:41,600 --> 00:14:42,866
Way more than you pay for.

287
00:14:43,200 --> 00:14:44,433
You can try before you buy.

288
00:14:44,500 --> 00:14:45,500
You won't lose out.

289
00:14:46,200 --> 00:14:47,200
Well?

290
00:14:48,866 --> 00:14:51,933
Then… a three-day trial period.

291
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:53,000
A trial period?

292
00:14:53,433 --> 00:14:55,300
Did you not say try before you buy?

293
00:14:55,666 --> 00:14:57,000
If I am not satisfied

294
00:14:57,100 --> 00:14:58,765
I can let you go at any time.

295
00:14:58,766 --> 00:14:59,766
No problem!

296
00:14:59,900 --> 00:15:00,900
Deal!

297
00:15:01,366 --> 00:15:01,900
Tell me.

298
00:15:02,366 --> 00:15:03,400
What do you need done?

299
00:15:03,633 --> 00:15:05,033
I can show off right now.

300
00:15:06,466 --> 00:15:08,666
Then start with the laundry I've piled up.

301
00:15:10,133 --> 00:15:11,133
No problem.

302
00:15:14,933 --> 00:15:17,000
Oh right! Where's the washing machine?

303
00:15:20,066 --> 00:15:21,566
I don't like machine washing.

304
00:15:21,900 --> 00:15:23,565
The washboard is in the bathroom.

305
00:15:23,566 --> 00:15:25,900
A washboard? By hand?

306
00:15:25,966 --> 00:15:26,600
What?

307
00:15:26,866 --> 00:15:28,066
Can't you handle that?

308
00:15:28,800 --> 00:15:29,800
I can handle it!

309
00:15:30,333 --> 00:15:31,166
In Singapore

310
00:15:31,333 --> 00:15:32,500
everyone washes by hand.

311
00:15:33,166 --> 00:15:34,166
I'm on it.

312
00:16:10,600 --> 00:16:11,600
Hey!

313
00:16:11,800 --> 00:16:12,800
Careful!

314
00:16:15,133 --> 00:16:16,565
I told you to call me!

315
00:16:16,566 --> 00:16:18,533
What if you cut yourself on the glass?

316
00:16:24,200 --> 00:16:25,200
Are you okay?

317
00:16:26,533 --> 00:16:27,832
Don't touch me!

318
00:16:27,833 --> 00:16:28,833
Okay!

319
00:16:29,066 --> 00:16:30,133
Then don't move.

320
00:16:30,666 --> 00:16:32,133
It's all broken glass here.

321
00:16:32,300 --> 00:16:34,066
I just don't want you getting hurt.

322
00:16:34,300 --> 00:16:35,933
From now on let me do it.

323
00:16:36,533 --> 00:16:38,633
I'm not a free carer, you know.

324
00:16:38,900 --> 00:16:40,166
So don't hold back.

325
00:16:57,266 --> 00:16:58,266
Whoa!

326
00:16:58,866 --> 00:16:59,866
What is it?

327
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:02,000
So this is what you

328
00:17:02,133 --> 00:17:03,333
spent half the day on?

329
00:17:06,300 --> 00:17:07,300
Not bad at all.

330
00:17:08,233 --> 00:17:09,566
That's none of your business.

331
00:17:10,733 --> 00:17:11,333
I'm hungry.

332
00:17:11,666 --> 00:17:12,233
Perfect.

333
00:17:12,333 --> 00:17:13,333
I'm hungry too.

334
00:17:13,900 --> 00:17:14,266
Takeout.

335
00:17:14,333 --> 00:17:15,800
I don't like takeout.

336
00:17:16,366 --> 00:17:17,966
The ingredients are in the fridge.

337
00:17:18,300 --> 00:17:19,333
The door is that way.

338
00:17:20,666 --> 00:17:21,666
Come on.

339
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:23,100
It's just cooking.

340
00:17:23,200 --> 00:17:24,200
It's my specialty.

341
00:17:24,400 --> 00:17:25,166
Tell me

342
00:17:25,333 --> 00:17:26,333
what do you want?

343
00:17:26,600 --> 00:17:28,466
Chinese, Japanese, or Western?

344
00:17:30,833 --> 00:17:31,833
It doesn't matter.

345
00:17:33,100 --> 00:17:33,766
Hey.

346
00:17:34,100 --> 00:17:35,633
Don't move. There's broken glass.

347
00:17:36,266 --> 00:17:37,865
Let go. Who told you to touch me?

348
00:17:37,866 --> 00:17:39,000
I'm your caregiver now.

349
00:17:39,066 --> 00:17:40,700
On the clock, you answer to me.

350
00:17:41,033 --> 00:17:42,232
Let go. Ah—.

351
00:17:42,233 --> 00:17:42,733
Come here!

352
00:17:42,734 --> 00:17:44,099
Let go of me!

353
00:17:44,100 --> 00:17:44,800
Don't move!

354
00:17:45,100 --> 00:17:46,100
Sit still.

355
00:17:46,833 --> 00:17:48,800
Hey! Song Yi! I'm warning you!

356
00:17:48,966 --> 00:17:50,833
If you touch me again, I'll…

357
00:17:51,266 --> 00:17:52,266
You'll what?

358
00:17:53,333 --> 00:17:54,333
Fire me?

359
00:17:55,100 --> 00:17:57,733
Do not think you are safe
just because Yong Qi is here.

360
00:17:57,800 --> 00:18:00,033
If I want you dismissed,
no one can help you.

361
00:18:01,400 --> 00:18:06,066
I'm doing my job as a
caregiver. A full-time one.

362
00:18:06,300 --> 00:18:08,165
How could I not touch you?

363
00:18:08,166 --> 00:18:09,566
So for these three days,

364
00:18:09,733 --> 00:18:11,633
you'd better get used to it.

365
00:18:11,719 --> 00:18:13,851
I'll look after you like my own brother.

366
00:18:13,888 --> 00:18:14,928
I'm not your damn brother.

367
00:18:14,966 --> 00:18:15,966
Watch your mouth.

368
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:17,166
My mouth behaves itself.

369
00:18:18,200 --> 00:18:18,733
Unlike you.

370
00:18:18,866 --> 00:18:20,033
You don't mean a word.

371
00:18:20,333 --> 00:18:21,333
Playing it cold.

372
00:18:21,573 --> 00:18:24,373
- You'll end up with no friends.
- Understand this.

373
00:18:24,800 --> 00:18:26,400
You are a temporary caregiver.

374
00:18:26,633 --> 00:18:28,500
My friends are not your concern.

375
00:18:28,566 --> 00:18:29,566
Xu Feiyu.

376
00:18:30,300 --> 00:18:31,466
You always like this?

377
00:18:32,933 --> 00:18:33,933
Like what?

378
00:18:36,066 --> 00:18:37,066
Just…

379
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:39,200
scared of strangers.

380
00:18:39,433 --> 00:18:41,933
You are insane! You—.

381
00:18:42,200 --> 00:18:43,633
Do your job and nothing else.

382
00:18:43,700 --> 00:18:46,232
We are not close. Do not cross the line.

383
00:18:46,233 --> 00:18:47,233
Fine.

384
00:18:47,633 --> 00:18:51,166
Then let's get close as fast as we can.

385
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:53,333
Song Yi!

386
00:19:08,600 --> 00:19:09,600
Dad!

387
00:19:10,200 --> 00:19:11,733
I'm only doing this for you.

388
00:19:12,366 --> 00:19:15,666
Otherwise I'd pull his pants down
and beat him senseless!
